# Example ReRDMFT input file: water, STO-3G, MULLER_AS (the antisymmetric Muller functional),
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE with ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO (Utils/NEO.h) instead of the default ADAM --
# the NEO counterpart of water_muller_as_full_optimization.inp, same system, same functional.
# ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO: the orbital-rotation step of each macro-iteration is a second-order,
# matrix-free, trust-region Newton step (targeting the ground state only, no saddle-point search)
# instead of ADAM's many small first-order steps; the Hessian-vector product never forms the
# dense orbital-rotation Hessian (Full_opt/FullOptimization.h's RdmftModel::hessian_vector).
# NEO needs the dense two-electron integrals (falls back to ADAM, with a printed note, under
# CHOLESKY TRUE) and, for X2C, its Newton steps are additionally restricted to the
# time-reversal-symmetric (Kramers) subspace exactly like ADAM's own restriction.
# Typically converges in far fewer macro-iterations than ADAM (a handful, not tens), but is NOT
# guaranteed to land on the SAME stationary point for every PNOF/GNOF system -- compare against
# the ADAM run (water_muller_as_full_optimization.inp) as a routine cross-check; JK_only
# functionals like MULLER_AS have not shown this sensitivity in testing.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL MULLER_AS
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
